WEBVTT

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.500
I might've overestimated our chances here.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.960
I'm still too weak.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:20.130
I want to learn how to use your powers better.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:21.500
Fran…

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.000
So I won't stop.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.080
I need more tough fights like these…

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.460
…to get stronger!

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.540
I won't get stronger if I run away!

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.710
I've been so focused on protecting Fran.
I was too scared of her getting hurt.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:02.750
But Fran doesn't want borrowed power.
She doesn’t just want to LOOK strong.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:12.830
She wants to toe that dangerous line, to endure
and overcome pain and injury, to obtain true strength!

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.580
Fran is already committed to a tough journey.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.880
Teacher, cover me!

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.460
So I've gotta commit, too!

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.290
I'll watch your back!

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:28.000
You take on whatever comes at you
from the front and slice 'em down!

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:28.830
Mmkay!

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:29.710
Let's go!

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.460
Heavy Slash!

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:42.540
Middle Heal!

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.080
You okay?!

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.170
Yeah, I can keep going!

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:50.630
Okay, then go!

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:54.830
Stronger...

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.670
I'm gonna get stronger!

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.330
Fran's not just a weak little kitten.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.380
She's baring her fangs to fight for her dreams.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.170
She's a proper beastman!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.670
Fran has reached Level 12.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.040
My little Fran is so amazing!

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:21.880
<b>EPISODE 4:</b>

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:21.880
<b>THE TERRIFYING GOBLIN STAMPEDE</b>

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.000
Whoa now, the hell happened?!

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.830
You're looking worse for wear!

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:27.380
The hell were you two fighting to get like this?

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.920
Goblins.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.420
How many were you up against to get like this?

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:34.540
One, two… a lot.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.420
Cut down over a hundred.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.040
Over a hundred?!

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:43.500
Sorry to hit you up again so quickly, Garrus,
but could you fix up her armor?

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.710
Yeah, I can do that for ya.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:51.290
Two days from now, Fran's gonna take on
her first dungeon to take out the goblins.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.210
What?!

00:04:58.290 --> 00:04:59.710
There's the goblin hideout.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:01.880
Should I go in?

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.670
No, not yet. The sun's setting and you're exhausted.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.880
And there's going to be way more of them in there, too.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:09.540
Okay.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:13.290
Let's go collect the crystals
from back where we were and head into town.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.210
Absorb Crystal!

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.750
Fran! It's me!

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:36.880
Damn, look at all these dead goblins…
You killed these all by yourself?

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:37.670
Uh-huh.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:42.080
Hold on, if that's true,
you're at least a D-Rank adventurer.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.960
I found a goblin hideout over there.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:49.250
It can't be...

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.080
This cave wasn't here a month ago.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:58.380
So this isn't just a hideout.
It's probably a full-blown dungeon.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:00.210
What's the difference?

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:04.460
Dungeons will pop up out of nowhere.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:08.540
Fran, the guildmaster will probably
want to hear your account.

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.170
Would you go back to town to see him?

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.130
I could. But...

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:17.210
Don't worry. We'll keep an eye
on this area while you're gone.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:18.710
Okay.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:27.880
Didja really kill a whole horde
of goblins and hobgoblins?!

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.580
How many goblins did you kill?!

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.920
How many hobgoblins?!

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.380
A lot?

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.580
How many is a lot?!

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.330
Calm yourself, Donadrond.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.330
Fran, would you mind describing the details
of your encounter in more tangible terms?

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.920
It was around 130.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.130
Around 130?

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:53.170
And about 20 higher-tier ones.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.170
And about 20 higher-tier ones.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:59.420
What?! That's a tell-tale sign
that a goblin stampede's about to occur!

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:03.250
Did any of the goblins attempt
to retreat during the battle?

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:05.540
No, they fought me till the end.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.500
We've found ourselves in dire circumstances, then.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:15.500
Not retreating means they could not
retreat back to their hideout anymore.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:21.290
The one you discovered
is likely full of stronger, higher-tier monsters.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.080
This ain't good…

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:28.040
The dwarf guy said it wasn't a hideout anymore,
it was a dungeon.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.170
Really?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.580
Then we need to gather
a proper hunting party to deal with them.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:38.580
Issue an urgent call for any adventurers Rank F or above.

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:39.580
Yes, sir!

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:43.960
Now, Miss Fran, we would like you to accompany us.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:46.710
While we wish this could come
under better circumstances,

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.080
we would like to promote you to Rank F.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:51.170
For real?

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.250
But I haven't done enough quests yet.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:01.040
The only strong adventurer in Alessa at present
is Donadrond, who is Rank C.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:04.000
We haven't time to wait for you to fulfill the prerequisites.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:09.880
Besides, after defeating a goblin horde
of that size on your lonesome,

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:13.500
we can hardly allow you to remain
as a mere G-Rank adventurer.

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.080
So that's the story.

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.540
Rankin' up pretty fast, huh?

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:21.250
Repair!

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.380
Is that a restoration spell?

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:31.580
Yep! You're good now.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:32.920
It's fixed already?

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:40.210
I can use these mana crystals as catalysts
while casting to return it nearly to its original state.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.880
It's an Arcane Blacksmith skill.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:46.880
Wow. That's pretty nifty. How much'll it cost us?

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:51.790
About 10,000 gold. Same price as the crystals.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.790
That's cheaper than I thought.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:09:01.080
Know the more times you fix it,
the harder it gets to restore, so you'll need more catalyst.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.920
Next one will cost you around 30,000.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:07.580
Makes sense. Gets less efficient to repair.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:10.080
Garrus, what's a dungeon like?

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:13.170
Right, this'll be your first time.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:20.630
Dungeons are created by
the God of Chaos as trials for mankind,

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:23.170
which is, they just pop up out of the blue.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:28.250
More specifically, a Dungeon Core spawns,

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:35.670
and the monster closest to it becomes
the Dungeon Master and a servant of Chaos.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:44.000
The INT and WIS of the Dungeon Master
determines the dungeon's design.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:50.380
Old dungeons have unique ecosystems
that play host to rare monsters,

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:55.750
and you can often find precious metals
and enchanted items in older dungeons, too.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:02.710
You could say that's Chaos' way
of rewarding us for completing the trial.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:04.080
Here.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:07.630
So is this Chaos god a good god?

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:10.790
You could see it that way.

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:15.540
I can't put it on by myself.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.130
C'mon.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:22.960
Welp, with this one bein' so new,
you probably won't find much good treasure in it.

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:25.080
Thanks, Garrus.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.290
Of course.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.750
Oh, right. Teacher?

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.380
Hm?

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:34.000
I'll have your scabbard ready for you
the day you set out for the dungeon.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:36.330
Really?! Thanks!

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:41.880
Bye-bye.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.920
Good luck killin' those goblins.

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:45.630
Mm-hmm.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:54.420
Dang! Your stats have gone up like crazy!

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>Name: Fran</b>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>Age: 12</b>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>Race: Beastman, Black Cat</b>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>Class: None</b>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>LV: 12</b>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>VIT:</b>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>AGI:</b>

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>INT:</b>

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>STR:</b>

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.380
Is that 'cause you took the Spellsword class?

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:05.960
<b>Titles:       Master Dissasembler</b>

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:05.960
<b>Healing Mage</b>

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:05.960
<b>Skill Collector</b>

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:05.960
<b>Flame Wielder</b>

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:05.960
<b>Master Cook</b>

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:05.960
<b>Battle-Worn</b>

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:05.960
<b>Goblin Killer</b>

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:05.960
<b>Executioner</b>

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.000
You even got yourself three titles!

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:05.960
Let's see. Goblin Killer;
you get that after killing 100 goblins…

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:09.250
And it boosts your stats, too? Damn.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:19.080
Healing magic is pretty mentally exhausting, huh?

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:24.380
Good work today, Fran. You can relax now.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:26.830
I wanna take a bath.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.920
Okay, see you after, then.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:30.250
I want you to come, too.

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:31.380
What?!

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:36.330
Let's take a bath together.
You got lots of blood on you and need to be cleaned.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:41.250
N-no, I'm fine! I wanna take a look at my skills, anyway…

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:43.420
Hey! Stop!

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:43.420
No, you're coming.

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:45.880
Whoa, c'mon, stop!

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:52.380
It's huge!

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:58.000
Here I thought cats were supposed to hate water…

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.960
You like taking baths, Fran?

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:03.420
Yeah. I do.

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.130
My mom and I took baths together.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:07.880
Is that right?

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.000
How's it feel, Teacher?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.880
O-oh, fine!

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.670
Hold it right there!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:16.460
Did you bring your weapon into the bath?!

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.500
What terrible manners!

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:22.290
N-NELL?!

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.080
So good!

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:38.790
This inn is affiliated with the guild.
Myself and the other assistants have rooms here.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:44.330
More importantly, Fran,
you can't take your sword into the bath!

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:49.580
Sorry. We worked hard together
so I wanted to give him a bath.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:52.540
All right.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:57.790
Oh, yes! I heard you were joining the party
to clear out the goblin dungeon.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.380
Uh-huh. I'm gonna fight hard.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.540
It's your first dungeon, right?

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:05.420
I know you're a toughie, but be careful, okay?

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:07.670
Thanks, Nell.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:12.130
Ugh. I'm so angry at that awful lieutenant…

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:16.460
With the Knights Brigade refusing to help,
the adventurers have to shoulder all the burden!

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:17.790
The Knights Brigade?

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:18.500
Yes.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:22.540
Their Lieutenant Allsand is a nobleman
who hates adventurers,

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:25.460
and he's the one who turned down our request for aid.

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:29.380
He's absolutely useless! I wish he'd piss off and die!

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:32.710
Nell's got some pent-up rage…

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.420
If only Amanda were here.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.420
Amanda? I heard that name somewhere.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.500
I think Randell mentioned her.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:45.250
Her full name and title is A-Rank Adventurer,
Amanda the Great Mother.

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:47.460
She's the ace of the Alessa guild.

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:53.170
But she and the other high-ranks are checking out
the disturbance on the Greatwolf Plain.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:56.290
I didn't think my rampage would cause all this…

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:59.960
Ugh, of all the times for a new dungeon to pop up…

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.580
Chaos is really causing us, well, chaos.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.920
What kind of god is Chaos?

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:10.210
Good question. I can tell you
what I know from what I've read…

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.630
The gods came to our realm from another world.

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:16.250
The ten strongest came first.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:24.000
Of them, the gods of the Sun, Moon,
Oceans, Earth, Fire, Storms, Forests, and Beasts,

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.080
created the world and the life within it.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:32.710
The god of the Dead created the Great Wheel of
Reincarnation, upon which the world began to turn.

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:40.880
Later on, their 78 children
would make their own marks on the world.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:45.960
The last of the Ten Great Gods is the Goddess of Chaos.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:50.960
To keep the world in balance,
and give humanity the strength to persist,

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:55.580
the Goddess introduced chaos to the world.

00:14:56.170 --> 00:15:00.710
Her trials, or dungeons, as we know them,
are but one of her many machinations.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.580
So the god of Chaos is a goddess...

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.670
So is the Goddess of Chaos good?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.790
That's difficult to say.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:12.210
Oh, wait, why isn't there a God of War?

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:16.580
There is… or should I say, there was.

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:21.170
The God of War was so addicted
to power that he fell to Evil.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.420
Evil?

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:29.710
After the God of War fell, he gained incredible power
and tried to use it to subjugate the other gods.

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:36.380
But he was defeated, split apart,
and his pieces sealed and scattered across the world.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:44.710
The parts of him that were not sealed away
created Fiends, like goblins and orcs.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:46.960
This is good stuff to know.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:52.080
So the Fiend race I saw with Identify
are all descendants of that evil god.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:53.130
Huh?

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:57.040
Fran, are you okay?!

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:07.790
Her mind and body are tired after the day's excitement.

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:13.250
This world is in such close contact with the gods…

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:16.290
Another reminder that it's nothing like my old one.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.290
Excuse me!

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.920
Garrus, we're here!

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:28.790
Hey, there you are. Take this with you today.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.710
Whoa! Is this my scabbard?

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:34.250
It looks real cool!

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:36.920
Teacher?

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:40.580
Yeah! Lemme get right in…

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:46.540
WHOA!

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:49.880
It feels so nice! Holy crap!

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:54.170
Damn, Garrus, this is awesome!

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:58.380
I'm glad ya like it.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:00.420
You sound so happy, Teacher.

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:02.670
Yeah, 'cause it's a nice-ass scabbard!

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:05.250
It's not just a scabbard, either.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:07.710
It's got a special feature, too.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:09.500
Whoa, really?

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.830
See this metal bit here?

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:12.580
Uh-huh.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:15.290
If you pull it like this…

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:25.330
You can use your Telepathy
to unsheathe yourself all on your own.

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:26.420
Nifty!

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.290
Thanks, Garrus!

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:33.960
You got it, Teacher and Fran.
Good luck on your first dungeon crawl!

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:36.500
Mm-hmm!

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.250
I'm gettin' pumped up.

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.830
Show 'em what you're made of, Fran!

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.710
I can't wait to go in the dungeon.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.210
Attention, everyone!

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:55.170
This afternoon, we're headed out
to find and eradicate a large goblin threat!

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.130
Donadrond is heading the party, huh?

00:17:58.330 --> 00:18:02.960
The familiars that scouted the dungeon
have confirmed this cave is overrun with goblins,

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:10.210
and with their numbers, we're on the brink
of encountering a goblin stampede!

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.290
Our first objective:

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:18.000
Stop the stampede by killing the Goblin King and Queen!

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:23.420
Then, if possible, explore the dungeon
and bring it under guild control!

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:26.710
That means killing the Dungeon Master!

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:28.920
The Dungeon Master…

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:32.250
We'll set up a temporary base of operations here…

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:34.670
What was that?!

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:39.540
They're coming! The goblins are rushing out!

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:40.500
What?!

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:43.500
They barely made a peep yesterday!

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:47.040
C'mon, you lot! Don't scatter! Hold your ground!

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:53.330
This isn't good.

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:57.540
We're supposed to work as a team,
but the adventurers are scattering apart…

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:02.580
Are the goblins intentionally trying to split us up?

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:04.880
There are hobgoblins attacking, too.

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:08.500
Yeah, and the adventurers think they're just
regular goblins. They're gonna get slaughtered!

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:11.750
Fran! Let's help them out
and head towards the mouth of the cave!

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:12.630
Mm-hmm!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:16.290
Hey!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:21.290
Newbie! Don't go rushing in by yourself!

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:31.420
Is this because she has the Goblin Killer title?

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:36.170
Do they see Fran as some kind of horrible demon?

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:43.710
Let's go!

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.500
Thanks, I owe you!

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:55.710
Mm-hmm.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:20:00.000
Fran, let's hold off on absorbing crystals.
We'll draw too much attention to ourselves.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:02.790
We won't draw too much attention
to ourselves inside the cave.

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:03.880
That's right!

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:07.210
This situation will make it hard to get in there, though.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:12.330
All right, Fran. I know you're still practicing,
but think you can give it a shot?

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.330
Mm-hmm. I'll try!

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:21.250
This is the skill I got from the Tyrant Saber-Tooth:

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.330
Air Leap!

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:25.000
Whoa…

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.080
The hell?

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:27.380
Is that Fran?!

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:33.830
She's insane… Air Leap is a unique skill
for high-tier classes!

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:35.830
Teacher, use magic!

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:40.460
Okey-dokey, here we go!

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:43.710
Fire Magic: Tri-Explosion!

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:46.920
She can use fire magic, too?!

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:51.880
Sword Art: Sonic Wave!

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:01.790
The goblins are all bunched up in there.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:03.380
Now's our chance!

00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:07.040
Time to use high level fire magic: inferno magic!

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:10.920
Flare Blast!

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.210
Nice, Teacher!

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:20.170
Sh… she made us a path…

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:24.540
Donadrond should be able
to take out the goblins behind us.

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:27.630
Okay, let's get into the dungeon!

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:29.000
Mm-hmm!

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:31.080
Wha-?! Fran?!

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:35.830
Sorry to step on your veteran feet,
but Fran's gonna finish 'em all!

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:38.710
I'll kill the King and Queen, too!

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:48.040
The surprise attack has the humans in a panic!

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:50.500
And on top of that…

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:55.130
Our random monster summoning
brought us the strongest class of monster!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:59.790
No one will be able to defeat our dungeon,
the Goblin Empire!

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>NEXT EPISODE</b>

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>THE FEEBLE FIRST DUNGEON</b>
